# Prosthetic Sleep Consolidation
# Offline replay network for consolidation after waking grasp episodes.
# Sensor replay and supervisory interneuron both drive actuator consolidation.

Define a network named prosthetic_sleep with timestep 0.0026.
# Network with 1 input, 3 LIF neurons, 2 linear transforms, 1 output.
# flow: input → sensor → actuator → output
#        interneuron ──────────→ actuator

# Layers:
Define an input port named input with shape (90,).
Define a LIF neuron named sensor with time constant 0.03, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.35.
Define a linear transformation named w_sensor_actuator with weight matrix shape (90, 90) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 42.
Define a LIF neuron named interneuron with time constant 0.02, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.25.
Define a linear transformation named w_interneuron_actuator with weight matrix shape (90, 60) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 43.
Define a LIF neuron named actuator with time constant 0.04, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.65.
Define an output port named output with shape (90,).

# Connections:
input connects to sensor.
sensor connects to w_sensor_actuator.
w_sensor_actuator connects to actuator.
interneuron connects to w_interneuron_actuator.
w_interneuron_actuator connects to actuator.
actuator connects to output.

# Note: STDP on sensor→actuator pathway is dropped — not representable in NIR.
# Future extension: add PES/STDP plasticity as metadata on w_sensor_actuator.
# Note: interneuron has no input port — it acts as an internal replay oscillator.
